  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py`. The full suite passes (24 tests). I didn't add your reproducer to the suite, so that run doesn't include `test_usage_outside_period_not_billed`.\n\nThe period filter was exclusive at both ends (`start < timestamp < end`). That dropped usage reported exactly at the period start, which is why your test got 0 instead of 5. The filter is now `start <= timestamp < end`. Usage at the start boundary counts in the period, and usage at the end boundary belongs to the next one, so it isn't billed twice.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
